      <abstract>The Congregational Church of Columbus, New York, was gathered in 1806. In 1814, a
        meeting house was constructed for the church. A parsonage for the church was built in 1842.
        The church dissolved in 1926. This collection includes church and society meeting minutes,
        financial records, Sunday school records, membership records, and disciplinary
        records.</abstract>
