    </acqinfo>
    <custodhist>
      <head>Custodial History</head>
      <p>Materials in this collection were given to the New York Conference of the United Church of
        Christ at an unknown time, likely following the church's dissolution. This collection was
        originally processed as part of the New York Conference records (RG0112) circa 1980.</p>
    </custodhist>
    <processinfo>
      <head>Processing Information</head>
      <p>This collection was processed by Zachary Bodnar, August 2026, according to the rules of
        Describing Archives: A Content Standard.</p>
    </processinfo>
    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>The Congregational Church of Columbus, New York, was gathered in 1806. In 1814, a meeting
        house was constructed for the church. That meeting house underwent major renovations and
        repairs in 1872, 1895, and 1903. A Sunday school for the church was organized in 1819. A
        parsonage for the church was built in 1842. The church dissolved in 1926.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>This collection contains administrative and select membership records for the church and
        society of the Congregational Church of Columbus in New York. This collection includes
        church and society meeting minutes, constitutions, financial records, Sunday school records
        and a catalog for the church's library, membership records, disciplinary records, and
        clippings from the church's centennial celebration.</p>
    </scopecontent>
    <arrangement>
      <head>Arrangement</head>
      <p>Materials in this collection have been arranged into chronological order by start date.</p>
    </arrangement>
